      },
      {
        "type": "heading",
        "attrs": {
          "level": 2
        },
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Method"
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "orderedList",
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "listItem",
            "content": [
              {
                "type": "paragraph",
                "content": [
                  {
                    "type": "text",
                    "text": "Heat the sugar in a heavy saucepan over medium heat without stirring. When it starts to melt at the edges, swirl the pan gently. Cook until it turns a deep amber colour."
                  }
                ]
              }
            ]
          },
          {
            "type": "listItem",
            "content": [
              {
                "type": "paragraph",
                "content": [
                  {
                    "type": "text",
                    "text": "Carefully add the fish sauce and coconut water. It will bubble and spit. Stir quickly until the caramel dissolves into the liquid."
                  }
                ]
              }
            ]
          },
          {
            "type": "listItem",
            "content": [
              {
                "type": "paragraph",
                "content": [
                  {
                    "type": "text",
                    "text": "Add the garlic, shallots, ginger, and chilli. Stir and cook for 2 minutes."
                  }
                ]
              }
            ]
          },
          {
            "type": "listItem",
            "content": [
              {
                "type": "paragraph",
                "content": [
                  {
                    "type": "text",
                    "text": "Gently lower the fish steaks into the pan in a single layer. Spoon the sauce over the top."
                  }
                ]
              }
            ]
          },
          {
            "type": "listItem",
            "content": [
              {
                "type": "paragraph",
                "content": [
                  {
                    "type": "text",
                    "text": "Reduce the heat to low. Simmer uncovered for 20 to 25 minutes, turning the fish once halfway through, until the sauce is thick and dark."
                  }
                ]
              }
            ]
          },
          {
            "type": "listItem",
            "content": [
              {
                "type": "paragraph",
                "content": [
                  {
                    "type": "text",
                    "text": "The sauce should cling to the fish. If it is still too liquid, increase the heat for the last few minutes."
                  }
                ]
              }
            ]
          },
          {
            "type": "listItem",
            "content": [
              {
                "type": "paragraph",
                "content": [
                  {
                    "type": "text",
                    "text": "Transfer to a serving dish or bring the pan to the table. Scatter with spring onion and serve with steamed rice."
                  }
                ]
              }
            ]
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "troubleshooter",
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "troubleshooterItem",
            "attrs": {
              "symptom": "The caramel burns before it reaches the right colour.",
              "cause": "The heat was too high.",
              "fix": "Use medium heat and watch the sugar constantly. Remove from heat the moment it turns amber. Residual heat will keep it cooking."
            }
          },
          {
            "type": "troubleshooterItem",
            "attrs": {
              "symptom": "The fish breaks apart when turning.",
              "cause": "The fish was moved too soon before a crust formed.",
              "fix": "Only turn the fish once, and do it gently with a wide spatula. A fish steak with skin holds together better than a skinless fillet."
            }
          },
          {
            "type": "troubleshooterItem",
            "attrs": {
              "symptom": "The sauce tastes too sweet.",
              "cause": "The caramel was not cooked dark enough.",
              "fix": "Cook the sugar to a deep amber, almost burnt colour. This gives bitterness that balances the sweetness."
            }
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "heading",
        "attrs": {
          "level": 2
        },
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Where this dish lives"
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Cá kho tộ is a Vietnamese home cooking classic eaten from north to south. "
          },
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "The clay pot version from the Mekong Delta is the most famous. "
          },
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Catfish from the delta rivers is the traditional choice of fish. "
          },
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Every Vietnamese mother has her own version of this dish. "
          },
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "It is a comfort food that most people associate with family dinners at home."
          }
        ]
      }
    ]
  }
